 # SGGX-based Precomputed Convolution
 
-Also called: SGGX-GGX convolution fit, SGGX-SG convolution fit
+Also called: SGGX-GGX convolution fit, SGGX-SG convolution fit, SGGX Convolution with SG/GGX Kernel
 
 ## Overview
-This method approximates the convolution of a SGGX microflake distribution with an isotropic spherical distribution (such as a GGX microfacet distribution or a Spherical Gaussian) as another SGGX distribution sharing the same eigenvectors. It solves the problem of efficiently computing the roughening effect of convolution in participating media by mapping the original roughness parameters to new parameters via a precomputed lookup table, avoiding expensive Monte Carlo integration at runtime. It builds on [Convolution of Aggregated Microfacet and Surface NDF](10871-convolution-of-aggregated-microfacet-and-surface-ndf.md).
+This method approximates the convolution of an SGGX microflake distribution with an isotropic spherical distribution (such as a GGX microfacet distribution or a Spherical Gaussian) as another SGGX distribution sharing the same eigenvectors [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently computing the roughening effect of convolution in participating media by mapping the original roughness parameters to new parameters via a precomputed lookup table, avoiding expensive Monte Carlo integration at runtime [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Convolution of Aggregated Microfacet and Surface NDF](10871-convolution-of-aggregated-microfacet-and-surface-ndf.md) [S1, unofficial].
 
